WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:19.068
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is July tenth. Summer in Japan means festivals and fireworks. Today's story is about one of Tokyo's most famous fireworks festivals, coming up later this month. Let's listen.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.620
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.088
<v News>夏のお祭りのニュースです。

00:00:27.788 --> 00:00:33.524
<v News>東京で、有名な花火大会が開かれます。

00:00:34.223 --> 00:00:43.392
<v News>名前は「隅田川花火大会」です。今年で49回目です。

00:00:44.091 --> 00:00:51.676
<v News>この花火大会は、7月25日の土曜日に行われます。

00:00:52.375 --> 00:00:58.304
<v News>時間は、夜の7時から8時半までです。

00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:06.108
<v News>花火は、隅田川の近くの2つの場所から打ち上げられます。

00:01:06.808 --> 00:01:12.471
<v News>全部で、およそ2万発の花火が上がります。

00:01:13.171 --> 00:01:19.603
<v News>毎年、100万人くらいの人が花火を見に来ます。

00:01:20.304 --> 00:01:26.688
<v News>浴衣を着て、お祭りを楽しむ人もたくさんいます。

00:01:27.388 --> 00:01:35.500
<v News>会場の近くは、とても混雑します。気をつけてください。

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.719
<v News>雨や風が強いときは、中止になります。

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.212
<v Host>Now let's break it down, sentence by sentence.

00:01:46.811 --> 00:01:52.956
<v Slow>東京で、有名な花火大会が開かれます。

00:01:53.756 --> 00:01:57.859
<v Host>In Tokyo, a famous fireworks festival will be held.

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:01.388
<v Vocab>花火大会

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:04.236
<v Host>It means a fireworks festival.

00:02:04.835 --> 00:02:07.067
<v Vocab>有名

00:02:07.468 --> 00:02:09.243
<v Host>It means famous.

00:02:09.843 --> 00:02:17.955
<v Slow>この花火大会は、7月25日の土曜日に行われます。

00:02:18.756 --> 00:02:23.243
<v Host>This fireworks festival takes place on Saturday, July twenty-fifth.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.147
<v Vocab>土曜日

00:02:26.548 --> 00:02:28.180
<v Host>It means Saturday.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.419
<v Vocab>行われる

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:34.532
<v Host>It means to be held or to take place.

00:02:35.132 --> 00:02:41.491
<v Slow>時間は、夜の7時から8時半までです。

00:02:42.292 --> 00:02:46.012
<v Host>The time is from seven in the evening until eight thirty.

00:02:46.611 --> 00:02:48.627
<v Vocab>夜

00:02:49.027 --> 00:02:51.379
<v Host>It means night or evening.

00:02:51.979 --> 00:02:59.611
<v Slow>花火は、隅田川の近くの2つの場所から打ち上げられます。

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:04.635
<v Host>The fireworks are launched from two places near the Sumida River.

00:03:05.235 --> 00:03:07.324
<v Vocab>場所

00:03:07.723 --> 00:03:10.027
<v Host>It means a place or location.

00:03:10.627 --> 00:03:13.147
<v Vocab>打ち上げる

00:03:13.548 --> 00:03:17.268
<v Host>It means to launch or set off, as with fireworks.

00:03:17.867 --> 00:03:23.939
<v Slow>全部で、およそ2万発の花火が上がります。

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:28.532
<v Host>In total, about twenty thousand fireworks go up.

00:03:29.132 --> 00:03:31.508
<v Vocab>全部で

00:03:31.907 --> 00:03:34.740
<v Host>It means in total or all together.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.379
<v Vocab>発

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.268
<v Host>It's the counter for shots or rounds, used here for fireworks.

00:03:42.867 --> 00:03:49.780
<v Slow>毎年、100万人くらいの人が花火を見に来ます。

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:55.235
<v Host>Every year, about one million people come to watch the fireworks.

00:03:55.836 --> 00:03:58.283
<v Vocab>毎年

00:03:58.683 --> 00:04:00.675
<v Host>It means every year.

00:04:01.276 --> 00:04:08.139
<v Slow>浴衣を着て、お祭りを楽しむ人もたくさんいます。

00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:13.788
<v Host>There are also many people who wear a light summer kimono and enjoy the festival.

00:04:14.388 --> 00:04:16.596
<v Vocab>浴衣

00:04:16.995 --> 00:04:21.220
<v Host>It means a yukata, a light cotton kimono worn in summer.

00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:24.172
<v Vocab>楽しむ

00:04:24.572 --> 00:04:26.300
<v Host>It means to enjoy.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:32.827
<v Slow>雨や風が強いときは、中止になります。

00:04:33.627 --> 00:04:37.180
<v Host>When the rain or wind is strong, it will be canceled.

00:04:37.779 --> 00:04:40.108
<v Vocab>中止

00:04:40.507 --> 00:04:43.987
<v Host>It means cancellation or calling something off.

00:04:44.588 --> 00:04:47.588
<v Host>Let's listen to the whole story one more time.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:51.956
<v News>夏のお祭りのニュースです。

00:04:52.656 --> 00:04:58.391
<v News>東京で、有名な花火大会が開かれます。

00:04:59.091 --> 00:05:08.259
<v News>名前は「隅田川花火大会」です。今年で49回目です。

00:05:08.959 --> 00:05:16.543
<v News>この花火大会は、7月25日の土曜日に行われます。

00:05:17.244 --> 00:05:23.172
<v News>時間は、夜の7時から8時半までです。

00:05:23.872 --> 00:05:30.975
<v News>花火は、隅田川の近くの2つの場所から打ち上げられます。

00:05:31.675 --> 00:05:37.339
<v News>全部で、およそ2万発の花火が上がります。

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:44.471
<v News>毎年、100万人くらいの人が花火を見に来ます。

00:05:45.172 --> 00:05:51.555
<v News>浴衣を着て、お祭りを楽しむ人もたくさんいます。

00:05:52.255 --> 00:06:00.367
<v News>会場の近くは、とても混雑します。気をつけてください。

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:06.588
<v News>雨や風が強いときは、中止になります。

00:06:07.288 --> 00:06:11.319
<v Host>Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:19.360
<v Slow>隅田川花火大会は、何月何日に行われますか。

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.399
<v Host>It takes place on July twenty-fifth, a Saturday.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.024
<v Slow>花火は、全部でおよそ何発上がりますか。

00:06:30.824 --> 00:06:33.680
<v Host>About twenty thousand fireworks in total.

00:06:34.279 --> 00:06:39.944
<v Slow>雨や風が強いときは、どうなりますか。

00:06:40.744 --> 00:06:42.735
<v Host>The festival is canceled.

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:54.136
<v Host>That's all for today. If you're in Tokyo on the twenty-fifth, look up and enjoy the show, and maybe try wearing a yukata too. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

00:06:54.735 --> 00:06:57.136
<v News>また明日。
